cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Codify: agent-native code graph with built-in version control"
message: "If you use Codify in your research or software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Andrew"
    affiliation: "Sidiora Labs"
  - name: "Sidiora Labs"
    website: "https://sidiora.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sidiora-labs/codify"
url: "https://github.com/sidiora-labs/codify"
abstract: >-
  Codify (cg) is a local-first code intelligence engine written in pure
  C11. It indexes a codebase into a queryable graph of symbols, call edges,
  and framework routes stored in a single SQLite database, layered with a
  content-addressed SHA-256 snapshot system for version control. It is
  designed for AI agents: a single context call returns entry points,
  matching symbols, callers, callees, and related routes, and a built-in
  MCP stdio server exposes the full engine, including a task engine for
  Ion kvx specifications. It adapts its worker pool and caches to the
  host machine, supports nineteen languages and over twenty web
  frameworks, and sends no data off the machine.
keywords:
